	abstract = {This paper presents Tendermint, a new protocol for ordering events in a distributed network under adversarial conditions. Tendermint proceeds in rounds, where each round has a dedicated proposer. The protocol simplifies the design of the PBFT SMR algorithm and the DLS algorithm for authenticated faults and achieves similar performance with fewer communication steps. We present a detailed description of the protocol, a formal proof of safety, an analysis of liveness, and experimental results.},
